> > Actually, it IS possible to start two different Nethack games on the
> > same user account, I remember having accidentally done it. You just
> > can't save both of them.

> Which makes it pretty much no then doesn't it? Due to the fact that
> nethack saves every level. It's been a while since I compiled, but

Not exactly. The level files in a unix faile can coexist for two games
started with the same user account, it's the SAVE files that can't.

> aren't the names of the lock files generated *from* the user/character
> name? Isn't there a way to choose character name separate from user
> name?

Not so. The lock files are alock.1, alock.2, alock.3 and so on when there
is no game running and the first player starts the game, block.1, block.2,
block.3 and so on for the second player, the third one gets files
starting with c and so on. Up to the number of players specified as
MAXNROFPLAYERS in the starting script.
If you don't believe THIS, just start a game with your usual user account
and check the names of the newest files in the playground dircectory.
Then, with that game going on, start another game with another user
account and chech the new files again. Save both games and load them again
in the other order, checking the names again after each load.

IIRC, you CAN use a character name different from the username with
the -u option in unix systems too, but I never use it and don't remember
if it affects the save file name and eliminates the save file conflict.

